hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1388","Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Zuhair told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, Al-Hakam told me, on the authority of a man called Al-Hanash, On the authority of Ali, Muhammad bin Yahya and Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, they said: Ahmad bin Yunus narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr narrated to us. Al-Hakam told me, on the authority of a man called Hanash, on the authority of Ali, Muhammad bin Yahya said, and this is the hadith of Ahmad, he said: “The sun was eclipsed and Ali prayed.” With the people, he started and recited with: Yaseen or something similar, then he bowed down to the length of the surah, then he raised his head and said: God hears those who praise Him, then He stood up for the duration of the surah, calling and saying “Allahu Akbar”, then he bowed for the duration of his recitation as well, so he mentioned the hadith, and said: Then he stood up in the second rak’ah, so he did the same as he did in the second rak’ah. The first rak’ah, then he told them that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.” Abu Bakr said in this report: He performed four rak’ahs, with each rak’ah like the report of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas."
